==Fight overview==
{{main|Demonic gorilla/Strategies}}

Demonic gorillas use all three [[combat style]]s to attack, and will change combat styles after missing three hits in that attack style. They are also capable of using [[protection prayers]], and will switch to the player's last used combat style against them when they have been dealt damage at least four times, and been dealt 70 or more damage. Therefore, players must bring at least two different combat styles to kill them. Though they have a 35% [[elemental weakness]] to [[water spells]], they are most often killed with melee and ranged.

The gorillas also have a special attack where they send a rock crashing down at the player's position, which can be easily avoided by moving one tile away from the current spot when the attack was initiated. If struck by this rock, the player will take 33% of their current health as damage; a single rock cannot kill the player by itself as a result.

'''({{Colour|red|Warning:}} The player can be hit by other players' rocks.)'''

Note that the gorilla's prayers '''can''' be bypassed through the use of [[Verac the Defiled's equipment|Verac's set]] but '''cannot''' be bypassed with [[special attacks]]. In addition, the healing effects of equipment like [[Guthan the Infested's equipment]] or [[Saradomin Godsword]] will still take place even through prayer, as well as the defence reduction from the [[Elder maul|Elder Maul]] and [[Dragon warhammer|Dragon Warhammer]]. Ironman accounts will not lose kill credit if another account applies the defence reduction '''if the gorilla is praying protect from melee.'''


When using Thralls in the fight, it is best to use the Thrall type that is of the style you did not bring. They will sometimes switch its prayer to match the Thrall damage type, saving a gear switch occasionally.

